  "ingredients": [
    "9 ounce boneless, skinless chicken breast",
    "1 tablespoon paprika",
    "1 tablespoon chili powder",
    "2 teaspoon salt",
    "2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1 teaspoon onion powder",
    "3/4 cup almond flour",
    "2 large egg",
    "1/2 cup hot sauce",
    "3 tablespoon butter",
    "1/4 cup olive oil",
    "3 tablespoon blue cheese (crumbled)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Pat your chicken breasts dry from any excess moisture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pound the chicken breasts using a meat hammer to flatten them to 1/2 inch thickness.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut the chicken breasts in half along the line of fat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a ramekin, combine the paprika, chili powder, salt, pepper, garlic powder, and onion powder.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, combine almond flour and 1/3 of the spice mix.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wrap foil around a cookie sheet and then place a cooling rack over the top. Season your chicken using 1/3 of the spices on one side of the chicken. Flip all of the halved breasts over and season the other side with your remaining spices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a container, whisk the eggs.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dip each chicken strip into the egg mixture, then into the almond flour and spices. Make sure both sides are covered. Lay them flat on the cooling rack.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a pan, add your hot sauce and butter on low heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-14.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Put your chicken into the oven for 15 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-16.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the chicken breasts finish cooking, take them out of the oven and drizzle one side with olive oil. Put them back in the oven for 3 minutes on broil. Flip the chicken breasts over, drizzling them with the remaining olive oil. Broil them again for 3 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/keto-buffalo-strips-17.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the chicken strips cool for 5 minutes, then serve with a side of sauce and blue cheese crumbles over them. You can optionally brush each chicken strip with the buffalo sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/superbowl-sunday-buffalo-strips/#wprm-recipe-50801-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
